{"question": "Why is France sending troops to guard a Saudi oil port?", "country": "SA", "voice_speed": 0.95, "gap": 0.36, "cover": ["HOUTHIS HIT SAUDI.", "FRANCE SENDS TROOPS.", "WHY YANBU?"], "region": "SAUDI ARABIA / RED SEA", "places": {"SANAA": {"id": "SANAA", "name": "Sanaa", "lat": 15.35, "lon": 44.21}, "RIYADH": {"id": "RIYADH", "name": "Riyadh", "lat": 24.71, "lon": 46.68}, "YANBU": {"id": "YANBU", "name": "Yanbu", "lat": 24.09, "lon": 38.06}, "TAIF": {"id": "TAIF", "name": "Taif", "lat": 21.27, "lon": 40.42}, "HORMUZ": {"id": "HORMUZ", "name": "Strait of Hormuz", "lat": 26.56, "lon": 56.25}}, "lines": [{"text": "Tonight, the Houthis say they fired missiles and drones at Riyadh, and at Aramco oil sites in Yanbu.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "Times of Israel, 24 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "flow", "from": "SANAA", "to": ["RIYADH", "YANBU"], "label": "Houthi claim: missiles + drones"}}, {"text": "Saudi Arabia says it shot down six ballistic missiles, aimed at Taif and Yanbu.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "Times of Israel, 24 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "TAIF", "head": "6 missiles intercepted", "notes": ["aimed at Taif + Yanbu", "damage: unconfirmed"]}}, {"text": "It's the second claimed attack on Riyadh in six days.", "src": [1, 0], "context": false, "note": "Middle East Eye / Times of Israel", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "RIYADH", "head": "2nd attack in 6 days", "notes": ["19 Sep: Riyadh", "24 Sep: Riyadh + Yanbu"]}}, {"text": "Within hours, France said it will send soldiers, radars and air defences to guard Yanbu.", "src": [2], "context": false, "note": "Reuters via Al-Monitor, 24 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "flight", "from": {"lat": 48.86, "lon": 2.35}, "to": "YANBU", "label": "French forces to Yanbu", "sub": "soldiers, radars, air defence"}}, {"text": "Macron says it's to protect the site, not to join the war.", "src": [2], "context": false, "note": "Reuters via Al-Monitor, 24 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "quote", "quote": "not to get us involved in any conflicts", "who": "Emmanuel Macron, 24 Sep", "flag": "FR"}}, {"text": "Britain had already agreed to give Saudi jets air-to-air refuelling.", "src": [3], "context": false, "note": "US News / Reuters, 21 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "statement", "lines": ["France: troops.", "UK: refuelling.", "Target: Yanbu."], "flag": "GB"}}, {"text": "So why Yanbu? Before the Iran war, over 100 ships a day sailed through Hormuz.", "src": [4], "context": false, "note": "DTN, 22 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "tankers", "mode": "before", "place": "HORMUZ", "lane": [[54.9, 26.15], [55.6, 26.35], [56.2, 26.55], [56.6, 26.42], [56.85, 25.9], [57.4, 25.45], [58.2, 25.2]], "head": "{n}+ ships a day", "n_from": 0, "n": 100, "notes": ["before the war"]}}, {"text": "Now traffic is down more than 90 percent.", "src": [4], "context": false, "note": "DTN, 22 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "tankers", "mode": "after", "place": "HORMUZ", "lane": [[54.9, 26.15], [55.6, 26.35], [56.2, 26.55], [56.6, 26.42], [56.85, 25.9], [57.4, 25.45], [58.2, 25.2]], "head": "down {n}%+", "n_from": 0, "n": 90, "notes": ["Iran war, month 7"]}}, {"text": "That makes Yanbu, on the Red Sea, Saudi Arabia's back door for selling oil.", "src": [2], "context": false, "note": "Reuters via Al-Monitor, 24 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "route", "from": "RIYADH", "to": "YANBU", "label": "The back door", "note": "Red Sea export route"}}, {"text": "And oil is already above 105 dollars a barrel.", "src": [5], "context": false, "note": "The National, 24 Sep 2026", "scene": {"type": "barrel", "value": "$105", "n": 105, "max": 125, "label": "Brent crude, per barrel", "detail": "24 Sep 2026", "ref": {"n": 70, "label": "PRE-WAR ~$70"}}}, {"text": "Hormuz is choked. Yanbu is under fire. If both close, where does the oil go?", "src": [], "context": true, "note": "", "scene": {"type": "statement", "lines": ["Hormuz: choked.", "Yanbu: under fire.", "What's left?"], "flag": "SA"}}], "sources": [{"n": 0, "outlet": "The Times of Israel", "title": "Houthis say they attacked Riyadh and Aramco facilities in Yanbu", "url": "https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/houthis-say-they-attacked-riyadh-and-aramco-facilities-in-yanbu/"}, {"n": 1, "outlet": "Middle East Eye", "title": "Houthis claim strikes on Riyadh, Yanbu while Saudi coalition says attacks thwarted", "url": "https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/houthis-claim-strikes-riyadh-yanbu-while-saudi-coalition-says-attacks-thwarted"}, {"n": 2, "outlet": "Reuters via Al-Monitor", "title": "France to send military to protect Saudi Arabia on Red Sea oil route, Macron says", "url": "https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/09/france-send-military-protect-saudi-arabia-red-sea-oil-route-macron-says"}, {"n": 3, "outlet": "US News / Reuters", "title": "UK's Burnham Agrees to Saudi Request for Refuelling Support", "url": "https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2026-09-21/uks-burnham-agrees-to-saudi-request-for-refuelling-support"}, {"n": 4, "outlet": "DTN", "title": "Oil Below $100 Bbl as U.S.-Iran Diplomacy Awaited at U.N.", "url": "https://www.dtnpf.com/agriculture/web/ag/news/world-policy/article/2026/09/22/oil-100-bbl-u-s-iran-diplomacy-u-n-2"}, {"n": 5, "outlet": "The National", "title": "Oil prices top $105 as hopes fade for US-Iran breakthrough", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2026/09/24/oil-prices-top-105-as-hopes-fade-for-us-iran-breakthrough/"}], "caption": "The Houthis say they hit Riyadh and Aramco's Yanbu oil port tonight. Saudi Arabia says it downed 6 ballistic missiles. France is now sending troops, radars and air defences to guard Yanbu, Saudi Arabia's Red Sea back door while Hormuz is choked. If both close, where does the oil go?", "hashtags": ["saudiarabia", "houthis", "france", "oil", "outpost"]}